@prefix ag:   <http://example.org/agora#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

#  The version chain — APPEND-ONLY, and literally so: `agora-ratify` adds a node and never
#  rewrites a line. Which version is current is not stated here at all; it is DERIVED as the
#  one nothing else revises (vocabulary/agora/rules.ru), because a file that had to be edited
#  to record its own head would be a pointer with history attached rather than a chain.
#
#  Apart from world.ttl because a version's content hash covers world.ttl and hardware.ttl, and
#  cannot cover the file that states the hash. Mounted for agents, unlike hardware.ttl: an agent
#  must cite the version in force on every observation it records.
#
#  Each entry says WHO ratified it and in what capacity — the same qualified attribution the
#  world used to carry, now where it belongs, on the act rather than on the thing.
#
#  See agora/versions.py and knowledge/decisions/a-version-is-a-snapshot.md.

ag:version_1 a ag:WorldVersion ;
    ag:versionNumber 1 ;
    ag:contentHash "sha256:29a27b51522031a7ab734ac34bcdb7cde1b8f0e2cb270761dff103898d291a85" ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-09T17:35:45+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution [
        prov:agent <http://example.org/agora/user/dimonina> ; prov:hadRole ag:Sovereign ] .
